<!-- Compact homepage FAQ accordion (full-width) -->
<section id="faq" class="py-5 cf-faq-fullbleed">
  <div class="cf-faq-accordion">
    <div class="cf-faq-list">
      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q1">
        <summary>
          What makes CogniFocus different?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            CogniFocus is available now as an Android focus timer that pushes
            back when your attention drifts. Shield blocking, Goblin reactions,
            and recovery nudges make it feel active during a session instead of
            passive, with an iOS waitlist open for iPhone updates.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q2">
        <summary>
          How does Shield block apps during a session?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            During an active session, Shield watches for blocked apps and
            steps in before the scroll takes over. The Goblin reacts, and the
            session nudges you back toward work instead of letting the
            distraction loop win.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q3">
        <summary>
          Is CogniFocus good for ADHD or study focus?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            Yes. CogniFocus is built for study blocks, ADHD-friendly focus
            loops, and anyone who needs a gentler but firmer way to stay on one
            task.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q4">
        <summary>
          What happens when I drift or slip?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            If you slip into a blocked app or lose focus, recovery nudges help
            you come back without losing the whole run. The Goblin keeps the
            session honest, but one distraction does not have to end it.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q5">
        <summary>
          Why does CogniFocus need Android permissions?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            Usage Access lets CogniFocus see which app is in front so Shield
            can react. Display over other apps lets the Shield screen appear.
            Those permissions are used for focus protection, not for reading
            your content.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q6">
        <summary>
          What do Free, Pro, and Limitless include?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            Basic, or Free, covers the core focus loop with lighter limits.
            Pro expands the session tools with stronger Shield capacity,
            Manual Block, Planned Sessions, reminders, recovery nudges, and
            restore support. If a Limitless tier is offered later, its exact
            limits and extras will be listed on pricing before checkout.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="text-center mt-4">
    <a href="/faq.html" class="btn btn-glow cf-faq-view-all">
      View all FAQs ->
    </a>
  </div>
</section>
